Now, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-12)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-12)^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={4}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(12,-3)$ and its radius is $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-15468/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "697f9bd8-9edf-5643-8cdb-a821b6dce09c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15468"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
